+Allow sealed native-received quote intents to commit while an earlier send waits on the network. A queued result confirms local accepted identity and immutable source custody; the original single account worker still validates the current official profile and source before any submission. Insert-time ownership, logout epoch, accepted identity and source fences reject stale admissions without evicting a healthy sidecar connection. Profile-based quotes, mentions, ordinary text and protocol concurrency keep their existing paths.
