+
+### Native received quote admission
+
+For native-received sources, a queued reply confirms that its sealed source and
+reply were saved under the currently accepted account identity. Queue admission
+can run while an earlier send waits for its network response. It does not read
+or publish official profile files. The existing single account worker still
+checks the current profile, authorization and source before submission. Logout,
+changed ownership or identity, and recalled or quarantined sources prevent a
+stale new admission. Profile-based quote and mention admission keep their prior
+paths. Offline synthetic tests cover overlap, cookie refresh, replay, restart
+and official-format identity/publication/salt failures; this optimization has no
+new live latency or recipient-validation claim.
